## UniFi Controller Configuration (REQUIRED)
## Configure one or more UniFi controllers as a JSON array
## For UX7 and Dream Machine Pro controllers, use type="integrated"
## For standalone controllers, use type="standalone"

## Single Controller (UX7/Dream Machine)
UNIFI_CONTROLLERS=[{"url":"https://192.168.1.1","username":"admin","password":"your_password","type":"integrated","siteIdentifier":"default","enabled":true}]

## Multiple Controllers (Multi-Site Setup)
# UNIFI_CONTROLLERS=[{"url":"https://192.168.1.1","username":"admin1","password":"pass1","type":"integrated","siteIdentifier":"default","enabled":true},{"url":"https://192.168.2.1","username":"admin2","password":"pass2","type":"integrated","siteIdentifier":"site2","enabled":true}]

## Configuration Fields:
## - url: Controller URL with https:// (REQUIRED) - e.g., https://192.168.1.1 or https://unifi.example.com
## - username: Controller admin username (REQUIRED)
## - password: Controller admin password (REQUIRED)
## - type: "integrated" for UX7/Dream Machine or "standalone" for regular controllers (default: "integrated")
## - siteIdentifier: Site name in controller (default: "default")
## - enabled: true/false to enable/disable this controller (default: true)

## Important Notes:
## - All controller requests timeout after 5 seconds
## - The client receives success immediately when ANY controller succeeds
## - Remaining controller requests continue in the background
## - At least one controller must succeed for authorization to complete

## Other Configuration
SESSION_SECRET=secretString
AUTH=none
REDIRECTURL=/success.html
NODE_ENV=production
PORT=80
